# Text installer TTY / logging

`dialog` (ncurses) on the Live ISO runs on a Linux VT. It needs a real TTY on stdout/stderr for arrow keys and button focus.

## Required logging wrapper

```bash
# ✅ GOOD — script(1) allocates a PTY; dialog left/right works
if [ -z "$SCRIPT_LOGGED" ]; then
    export SCRIPT_LOGGED=1
    echo "" > "$LOG_FILE"
    exec script -f "$LOG_FILE" -c "$0 $*"
fi
```

```bash
# ❌ BAD — pipes steal the TTY; arrow keys echo as ^[[A/^[[B/^[[C/^[[D
if [ -z "$SCRIPT_LOGGED" ]; then
    export SCRIPT_LOGGED=1
    echo "" > "$LOG_FILE"
    bash "$0" "$@" 2>&1 | tee "$LOG_FILE"
    exit ${PIPESTATUS[0]}
fi
```

## Rules

- Never wrap the whole text installer (`installer-text.sh`) with `bash ... 2>&1 | tee` to capture logs.
- `frzr-bootstrap` / `frzr-deploy` may still use `| tee -a "$LOG_FILE"` for **command output only** (no interactive `dialog` on those fds).
- If log capture must change, prove arrow keys still work on a real VT (`openvt` + keyboard), not only inside a desktop PTY.
- Regression: after 2026-04-29 (`tee` wrapper) users could not left/right on the disk confirm yes/no; 3.18 (`script`) was fine. Fixed in installer-text.sh 2.1.4.

## Local repro / check

```bash
# Broken topology symptom on VT: flood of ^[[C/^[[D over the buttons
bash /tmp/dialog-verify/confirm_demo.sh tee
bash /tmp/dialog-verify/confirm_demo.sh script
```
